+# Marginalia Books
+
+A static website for Marginalia Books, a fictional independent bookshop on Chandler Lane in Wrenfield. It has a home page, a browsable catalogue with a genre filter, an events list, and a visit page with opening hours, directions and a contact form.
+
+Everything is plain HTML, CSS and vanilla JavaScript. There is no build step, no npm dependency and no network request to any other origin: no CDNs, web fonts, analytics or remote images. The site also works when `index.html` is opened straight from disk.
+
+## File layout
+
+```
+index.html        Home: introduction, staff picks, next events, calls to action
+books.html        Catalogue with a genre filter (state kept in ?genre=)
+events.html       Upcoming events in date order
+visit.html        Opening hours, address, directions, contact details and form
+css/styles.css    All styling (mobile-first, paper and ink palette)
+js/data.js        Books, events and shop contact details (edit content here)
+js/site.js        Shared helpers and the mobile menu
+js/home.js        Home page: staff picks and next events
+js/books.js       Catalogue filter, result count and URL state
+js/events.js      Events list with the upcoming filter
+js/visit.js       Contact form validation and demo submit
+tests/run.mjs    Headless Chromium tests for the acceptance criteria
+```
+
+Each page repeats the same header, navigation and footer markup. When you change one, change all four pages.
+
+## Viewing the site
+
+Any static server works. From the repository root, for example:
+
+```sh
+python3 -m http.server 8080
+# or
+npx http-server -p 8080 .
+```
+
+Then open http://localhost:8080/ in a browser. You can also open `index.html` directly from the file system.
+
+## Running the tests
+
+The tests use Playwright, which must already be installed globally. They start their own static server on a free port, load every page in headless Chromium and exit non-zero on any failure.
+
+```sh
+NODE_PATH=$(npm root -g) node tests/run.mjs
+```
+
+To run a subset, pass a part of a test name:
+
+```sh
+NODE_PATH=$(npm root -g) node tests/run.mjs --grep form
+```
+
+## Notes
+
+- The contact form has no backend. A valid submission says plainly that nothing was sent and offers a prefilled `mailto:` link to open in the reader's own email app.
+- All book and event content is invented. Prices are in pounds sterling.
